  "id": "dynamic-psychotherapy",
  "term": "dynamic psychotherapy",
  "definition": "Dynamic psychotherapy is a psychotherapeutic approach that works with unconscious emotions and conflicts, with attention to how these shape emotional responses, relationships, and bodily symptoms. It aims to help people recognize and work through avoided feelings and unresolved experiences that may be affecting current functioning.",
